---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Rawan Aladdin — For Thinkingbox"
  description="A targeted mini-portfolio: brand identity, digital design, and integrated campaign work by Rawan Aladdin, for the Thinkingbox Junior Designer role."
  bodyClass="tb-pitch"
  canonical="https://rawanaladdin.com/thinkingbox"
  noindex
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/thinkingbox.css" />
  </Fragment>

  <main>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ HERO ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="hero" class="tb-section" style="min-height: 100vh; justify-content: flex-end; padding-bottom: 8rem;">
      <p class="tb-hero-label">For Thinkingbox — August 2026</p>
      <h1 class="tb-hero-h1">Hi Thinkingbox,<br>I'm Rawan.</h1>
      <p class="tb-hero-sub">
        A designer who builds what she designs — brand identity, digital layouts,
        and the code that ships them.
      </p>
      <div class="tb-hero-links">
        <a href="mailto:hello@rawanaladdin.com" class="main-link">hello@rawanaladdin.com &#8599;</a>
        <a href="/projects.html" class="main-link">full portfolio &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="tb-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ WHY ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="why" class="tb-section">
      <p class="tb-section-label">Why me, specifically</p>
      <h2 class="tb-h2">Three things<br>I'd bring.</h2>
      <div class="tb-cards">

        <div class="tb-card">
          <p class="tb-card-num">01</p>
          <h3>I make the whole thing.</h3>
          <p>
            On Feeds I drew the identity, wrote the guidelines, applied them into the
            product myself in code, and produced the booth it launched from. Brand,
            product, print and motion — one project, one pair of hands.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tb-card">
          <p class="tb-card-num">02</p>
          <h3>I don't hand off at the interesting part.</h3>
          <p>
            I prototype in Figma and write the CSS and JavaScript that ships it. That
            means I know what a layout costs before I propose it, and I hand developers
            work that actually builds.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tb-card">
          <p class="tb-card-num">03</p>
          <h3>Range is the point.</h3>
          <p>
            Packaging, poster, editorial, merch, a nonprofit website, a shipped AI
            product, a booth. I move between formats without having to relearn how
            to think.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="tb-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════ PROJECT 01 — FEEDS ═══════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="feeds" class="tb-section">
      <p class="tb-section-label">Project 01 — Integrated</p>
      <div class="tb-project-head">
        <h2 class="tb-project-title">Feeds</h2>
        <span class="tb-meta">Brand Identity · Product UI · Launch Campaign · 2026</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tb-lede">
        A self-hosted reader and digest engine for developers. I didn't write the
        engine — an engineer I work with did — but more or less everything you can
        see, I made.
      </p>

      <div class="tb-tags">
        <span class="tb-tag">Brand Identity</span>
        <span class="tb-tag">Guidelines</span>
        <span class="tb-tag">Product UI</span>
        <span class="tb-tag">Front-end</span>
        <span class="tb-tag">Print</span>
        <span class="tb-tag">Motion</span>
        <span class="tb-tag">Environmental</span>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-detail">
        <div class="tb-detail-k">The identity</div>
        <div class="tb-detail-v">
          A four-point spark held between two curved strokes, and a wordmark set in
          lowercase Bricolage Grotesque — never capitalised, never reset. A five-colour
          palette built around one signature sage, specified down to the ratio each
          colour should occupy on a page, with an AA contrast floor. Delivered as an
          <strong>11-page guidelines document</strong> to the developer building the product.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-detail">
        <div class="tb-detail-k">Into the product</div>
        <div class="tb-detail-v">
          I applied the system myself, in CSS and JavaScript — the interface, the icon
          set, the Smart Inbox navigation, and a reskin of the digest email. I also
          rebranded the marketing site and re-recorded the product demo against the new UI.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-detail">
        <div class="tb-detail-k">The launch</div>
        <div class="tb-detail-v">
          Feeds launched from a live booth. I produced everything on and around the table:
          <strong>printed table runners, die-cut mark stickers in four colourways,
          business cards</strong>, a booth reel and a brand-identity reel looping on the
          screens, and the live product site.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-media">
        <img src="/feeds/feeds-booth.webp" alt="The Feeds booth during the showcase — table runners carrying the mark and tagline, a laptop looping the brand identity reel, and the live product site on the screen behind." loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="tb-caption">
        The booth, photographed during the showcase. Runners, stickers and cards were
        printed from the brand kit; both reels were cut for the screens behind the table.
      </p>

      <div class="tb-media-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="tb-media">
            <img src="/feeds/feeds-ui-articles.webp" alt="Feeds article list showing inline CVE, malware and actor chips extracted locally at view time." loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="tb-caption">The product UI after the brand refresh — I wrote this front-end.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="tb-media">
            <img src="/feeds/feeds-site-hero.webp" alt="The Feeds marketing site hero, rebranded around the brand kit." loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="tb-caption">Marketing site, rebranded against the same system.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="tb-note">
        Worth being precise about ownership: the Go engine, architecture and core product
        logic are the engineer's. The identity, the guidelines, the applied front-end, the
        email, the marketing site and the entire launch campaign are mine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="tb-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════ PROJECT 02 — ONWARD ═══════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="onward" class="tb-section">
      <p class="tb-section-label">Project 02 — Shipped product</p>
      <div class="tb-project-head">
        <h2 class="tb-project-title">Onward</h2>
        <span class="tb-meta">Product Designer &amp; Lead Developer · Sept – Dec 2024</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tb-lede">
        An AI interview coach for internationally educated healthcare professionals —
        nurses, mostly, arriving into a system that expects them to interview in a
        register nobody teaches them. I designed it and led the build.
      </p>

      <div class="tb-detail">
        <div class="tb-detail-k">The decision</div>
        <div class="tb-detail-v">
          Testing showed a practice tool that feels like a test just reproduces the
          anxiety it was meant to relieve. So we split the timer — elapsed in practice,
          counting down in mock — and reframed the real-time speech feedback as data
          rather than judgment.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-stats">
        <div>
          <div class="tb-stat-n">8/10</div>
          <div class="tb-stat-l">Ease of use, 12 users</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="tb-stat-n">200+</div>
          <div class="tb-stat-l">Presented to, live</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="tb-stat-n">4</div>
          <div class="tb-stat-l">Months to shipped</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-media">
        <img src="/ONWARD-main.webp" alt="The Onward dashboard — practice and mock interview entry points, saved resumes, and interview history." loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <div class="tb-cta-links">
        <a href="https://onward-p2.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="main-link">see it running &#8599;</a>
        <a href="/onward.html" class="main-link">read the case study &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="tb-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════ PROJECT 03 — SURFACE FIXER ═══════════════════════ -->
    <section id="surface-fixer" class="tb-section">
      <p class="tb-section-label">Project 03 — Client identity</p>
      <div class="tb-project-head">
        <h2 class="tb-project-title">Surface&nbsp;Fixer</h2>
        <span class="tb-meta">Brand Identity &amp; Website · Client</span>
      </div>
      <p class="tb-lede">
        Wordmark, visual direction and website for a cosmetic surface repair business —
        which happens to be my dad's. Working for family is its own category of client
        work: the notes come back faster and considerably less diplomatically.
      </p>

      <div class="tb-media">
        <img src="/surfacefixer-mockup.webp" alt="The Surface Fixer website hero shown on a laptop resting on concrete blocks." loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="tb-caption">
        The site, art-directed against the trade it serves.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="tb-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ STUDIO ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="studio" class="tb-section">
      <p class="tb-section-label">Studio work</p>
      <h2 class="tb-h2">Where I push<br>on typography.</h2>
      <p class="tb-lede">
        Self-directed and studio pieces. These are the ones where I answered only to
        the type.
      </p>

      <div class="tb-studio">
        <div class="tb-studio-item">
          <img src="/studio/metropolis.jpg" alt="Metropolis reissue poster — hand-drawn Deco letterforms above the Maschinenmensch, framed by period skyscrapers." loading="lazy" />
          <h4>Metropolis</h4>
          <p>Reissue poster. Letterforms drawn by hand — the O doubles as the Maschinenmensch's halo — with a full period credit block.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tb-studio-item">
          <img src="/studio/companion.jpg" alt="The Companion sparkling iced tea cans, with airmail borders, postage-stamp flavour marks and duotone city photography." loading="lazy" />
          <h4>The Companion</h4>
          <p>Packaging system built on one repeatable idea: every flavour is a destination. Airmail borders, stamp marks, bilingual EN/FR.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tb-studio-item">
          <img src="/studio/retrospect.jpg" alt="Ancient Retrospect — an editorial publication on the mosaics of the Hagia Sophia." loading="lazy" />
          <h4>Ancient Retrospect</h4>
          <p>Editorial design on the mosaics of the Hagia Sophia. Cover system, typographic hierarchy, full-bleed spreads.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-cta-links">
        <a href="/playground.html" class="main-link">more in the playground &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="tb-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ ABOUT / CTA ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="about" class="tb-section" style="min-height: 90vh;">
      <p class="tb-section-label">About</p>
      <h2 class="tb-h2">Let's make<br>something.</h2>
      <p class="tb-lede">
        Vancouver-based. I hold a Bachelor of Creative Industries and a Diploma in
        Digital Design &amp; Development, both from BCIT. Before that I studied
        cognitive science, philosophy and digital humanities at the University of
        Toronto — which is where I picked up the habit of asking how people actually
        think before deciding what they should see.
      </p>
      <p class="tb-lede">
        I'm early, and I'd rather say that plainly than inflate it. But I learn quickly,
        I can be handed a brand system and trusted not to break it, and I can carry a
        layout the whole way into the browser when that's useful.
      </p>

      <div class="tb-cta-links">
        <a href="mailto:hello@rawanaladdin.com" class="main-link">hello@rawanaladdin.com &#8599;</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rawan-aladdin" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="main-link">linkedin &#8599;</a>
        <a href="/projects.html" class="main-link">full portfolio &#8599;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="tb-footnote">
        Made for Thinkingbox — August 2026. Built in Astro, by me.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
